From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:36:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] network: spoof Neo architecture and bitness hints

Pin the base MacBook Neo's Apple A18 Pro architecture to arm and bitness
to 64 in shared persona constants. Use them in native NavigatorUAData
and quoted Sec-CH-UA-Arch / Sec-CH-UA-Bitness request headers rather than
reading the Linux host CPU or injecting JavaScript.

Extend the existing session-owned Device-Memory opt-in to independent
memory, architecture and bitness flags. Valid Accept-CH lists replace
the complete selection; missing/malformed lists preserve it. Reuse the
structured-list parser, origin/session lifecycle, trustworthy-origin and
self-policy gating, redirects, interception and cache response hooks.
Rename the memory-only state and hooks to reflect their expanded scope.

Recompute browser-generated headers after redirects and CDP changes,
preserving explicit higher-priority overrides. Keep Device-Memory: 8,
baseline brands/platform/full-version-list and all other hint behavior
unchanged. This is phase 0, not full Client Hints support: no new mobile,
model or platform-version headers, policy delegation or Critical-CH.

All 1658 existing development tests pass. Ignored runtime diagnostics
cover 63 architecture/bitness cases plus the prior 54 Device-Memory cases,
including native Promise/API shape and receiver rejection, worker values,
independent opt-in/replacement/reset, structured parameters, origin/session
isolation, insecure HTTP, redirects, CDP overrides and fulfillment, 304
responses and Vary cache transitions. No new upstream tests are added.

References:
https://www.apple.com/macbook-neo/specs/
https://developer.chrome.com/docs/privacy-security/user-agent-client-hints
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Sec-CH-UA-Arch
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Sec-CH-UA-Bitness
